<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/4th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wars of the Diadochi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/323-bce">323</a>–<a href="/years/281-bce">281 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Wars of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diadochi">Diadochi</a> were the conflicts fought between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a>'s generals, the Diadochi or successors, for control of his empire after his death, lasting from 323 to 281 BCE. They ended the unity of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macedonian-empire">Macedonian Empire</a>. Out of them emerged the Hellenistic kingdoms, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ptolemaic-kingdom">Ptolemaic Empire</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wars-of-the-diadochi.jpg" alt="Wars of the Diadochi" width="320" height="154" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: This vector image includes elements that have been taken or adapted from this file · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Diadochi_LA.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
